Per-node NCCL HCA override for start-deepseek-v4-flash-dspark.sh.

The upstream start script scp's .env.dspark to the worker verbatim and only overrides
NODE_RANK/HEADLESS/HF_CACHE/VLLM_HOST_IP per node. When the worker's RDMA HCA name differs
from the head's, NCCL_NET=IB fails on rank 1 ("NET/IB : No device found"). This adds the
worker's HCA (exact-match "=name:port" syntax) to the worker launch env, using the same
shell-env-beats-env-file compose interpolation mechanism the script already uses for
VLLM_HOST_IP. Replace rocep1s0f1 with your worker's HCA (see `ibv_devinfo`).

--- a/start-deepseek-v4-flash-dspark.sh
+++ b/start-deepseek-v4-flash-dspark.sh
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 echo "Starting DSpark worker on ${WORKER_HOST}..."
-ssh "$WORKER_HOST" "$REMOTE_COMPOSE NODE_RANK=1 HEADLESS=1 HF_CACHE='$WORKER_HF_CACHE' VLLM_HOST_IP='$WORKER_VLLM_HOST_IP' docker compose --env-file .env.dspark -f docker-compose.dspark.yml up -d"
+ssh "$WORKER_HOST" "$REMOTE_COMPOSE NODE_RANK=1 HEADLESS=1 HF_CACHE='$WORKER_HF_CACHE' VLLM_HOST_IP='$WORKER_VLLM_HOST_IP' NCCL_IB_HCA==rocep1s0f1:1 docker compose --env-file .env.dspark -f docker-compose.dspark.yml up -d"
